# Mettelo Code of Conduct

Welcome to Mettelo.

Thank you for being part of our community.

Mettelo exists to help data and AI professionals learn, build, contribute, and grow together through collaboration, open knowledge, and real-world impact.

This Code of Conduct outlines the standards of behaviour expected from everyone participating in the Mettelo ecosystem, including contributors, maintainers, mentors, volunteers, partners, employers, and community members.

By participating in any Mettelo project, discussion, repository, event, or platform, you agree to follow this Code of Conduct.

---

# Our Mission

Our mission is to build the world's most trusted ecosystem where data and AI professionals can:

- Learn continuously
- Build meaningful solutions
- Collaborate openly
- Share knowledge
- Demonstrate capability
- Create real-world impact

We believe that strong communities are built on professionalism, respect, inclusion, accountability, and generosity.

---

# Our Values

Every interaction within Mettelo should reflect our core values.

## Respect

Treat every community member with dignity, kindness, and professionalism regardless of their:

- Experience level
- Nationality
- Race
- Ethnicity
- Gender
- Disability
- Religion
- Sexual orientation
- Career background
- Opinions

Different perspectives strengthen our community.

---

## Collaboration

We encourage members to:

- Help others succeed
- Share ideas openly
- Review contributions constructively
- Build projects together
- Support beginners
- Celebrate community achievements

We believe collaboration creates greater impact than competition.

---

## Professionalism

Members should communicate professionally in:

- GitHub Issues
- Pull Requests
- Discussions
- Community forums
- Social media
- Events
- Meetings
- Documentation

Constructive disagreement is encouraged.

Personal attacks are not.

---

## Integrity

Be honest about:

- Your work
- Your experience
- Your contributions
- Your qualifications
- Your research
- Your project results

Never claim work that belongs to someone else.

Always give appropriate credit.

---

## Continuous Learning

Nobody knows everything.

We encourage curiosity, experimentation, asking questions, sharing lessons learned, and helping others improve.

---

# Expected Behaviour

Members are expected to:

- Be respectful in all communications
- Welcome newcomers
- Give constructive feedback
- Accept feedback professionally
- Credit contributors appropriately
- Follow repository guidelines
- Respect maintainers' decisions
- Protect confidential information
- Use inclusive language
- Help maintain a positive environment

---

# Unacceptable Behaviour

The following behaviours are not permitted within the Mettelo ecosystem.

## Harassment

Including but not limited to:

- Threats
- Intimidation
- Bullying
- Stalking
- Offensive comments
- Personal attacks

---

## Discrimination

Discrimination based on any protected characteristic is strictly prohibited.

---

## Hate Speech

Any form of hateful language or extremist content will result in immediate action.

---

## Spam

Including:

- Unsolicited advertising
- Excessive self-promotion
- Fake opportunities
- Referral scams
- Repeated posting

---

## Misrepresentation

Do not:

- Falsify project contributions
- Fabricate experience
- Misrepresent qualifications
- Claim ownership of another person's work

---

## Plagiarism

Always acknowledge original authors.

Respect software licences, datasets, documentation, and research.

---

## Malicious Activity

Never intentionally introduce:

- Malware
- Malicious code
- Security vulnerabilities
- Harmful scripts
- Copyright violations

---

# Community Standards

Every member should aim to:

- Teach generously
- Learn humbly
- Build responsibly
- Review fairly
- Communicate clearly
- Support others
- Leave projects better than they found them

---

# Reporting Violations

If you experience or witness behaviour that violates this Code of Conduct, please report it privately.

Email:

conduct@mettelo.com

Please include:

- Description of the incident
- Date and time
- People involved
- Supporting evidence (if available)

All reports will be handled confidentially wherever possible.

---

# Enforcement

Depending on the severity of the violation, Mettelo maintainers may take one or more of the following actions:

- Private warning
- Public warning
- Content removal
- Temporary suspension
- Permanent removal from repositories
- Removal from community platforms
- Revocation of contributor privileges

Serious violations may result in an immediate permanent ban.

---

# Scope

This Code of Conduct applies across the entire Mettelo ecosystem, including:

- GitHub repositories
- Discussions
- Issues
- Pull Requests
- Documentation
- Discord
- WhatsApp
- Events
- Workshops
- Community meetings
- Social media interactions conducted on behalf of Mettelo

---

# Our Commitment

Every contribution matters.

Whether you're fixing a typo, building an AI model, mentoring another member, or leading a project, your work helps strengthen the Mettelo ecosystem.

Together, we're building a community where professionalism, collaboration, and real-world impact come first.

Thank you for helping make Mettelo a welcoming place for everyone.

